 גארילקיויץ", "url": "https://www.hamichlol.org.il/%D7%90%D7%A0%D7%98%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%99_%D7%92%D7%90%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%A7%D7%99%D7%95%D7%99%D7%A5"}, {"title": "Anton Karl GRIES", "url": "https://gedbas.genealogy.net/person/show/1427731989"}, {"title": "Parish of St. Apostles Peter and Paul, Toruń", "url": "https://ecemetery.eu/en/cemetery/torun-nowy-cmentarz/grave/detail/3795353"}]}, "I couldn't find a record for Anton Grylewicz. The search returned no page with that exact name or a birth date for him.\n\nThe closest match is a Katyń victims database entry for a reserve lieutenant named Antoni Garmulewicz, whose date of birth is listed as 10 January 1891, in Wiktorowice near Miechów. The surname differs, so this may be a different person, and I'd verify it before relying on it.\n\nOther results with similar surnames are not the same person:\n- Tomasz Gryglewicz, an art historian, is listed as born in 1949 in Kraków, Poland.\n- Aleksander Gryglewski, a 19th-century painter, was born in Brzostek, and the date is given as 4 March 1833.\n\nFor Anton Grylewicz, try searching with alternate spellings (Gryglewicz, Grylewicz) plus a country or profession, or check genealogy databases and Polish or Belarusian archives."], "durationSeconds": 5.600852875, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01VozeN2chXcFp4iEJy9aKQ3", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
